---
import FaqList from '../../components/FaqList.astro';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { lineUrl, siteLines, siteSizes, sizeUrl } from '../../lib/data';
import {
  CHART_DATE, LOAD_INDEX_PATH, LOOKUP_PATH, REBATE_PATH, SPEED_RATING_PATH, blackFridayPath, cyberMondayPath, loadIndexPath, sizeCostPath, sizeMeaningPath, speedRatingPath,
} from '../../lib/paths';
import { LOAD_PAGES, SPEED_PAGES } from '../../lib/service-ratings';
import { EXACT_DATE, EXACT_PAGES, exactPath } from '../../lib/exact-match';
import { WAVE2_LINE_KEYS, WAVE2_SIZE_KEYS } from '../../lib/wave2';

const sizes = WAVE2_SIZE_KEYS.map((k) => siteSizes.find((s) => s.key === k)).filter((s): s is (typeof siteSizes)[number] => !!s);
const lines = WAVE2_LINE_KEYS.map((k) => siteLines.find((l) => `${l.brand_slug}/${l.line_slug}` === k)).filter((l): l is (typeof siteLines)[number] => !!l);
const warrantyPages = EXACT_PAGES.filter((p) => p.kind === 'warranty');
const mileagePages = EXACT_PAGES.filter((p) => p.kind === 'mileage');
const comparePages = EXACT_PAGES.filter((p) => p.kind === 'compare');
const rebatePages = EXACT_PAGES.filter((p) => p.kind === 'rebate');
const title = 'Exact Tire Size and Line Lookups';
const description = `Exact pages for mileage warranties, the highest UTQG grade by size, head-to-head treadwear, and November 2026 rebates. ${EXACT_PAGES.length} new query pages, read ${EXACT_DATE}.`;
const answer = `This page lists one URL per query. ${EXACT_PAGES.length} pages added ${EXACT_DATE} cover a maker mileage warranty, the highest NHTSA treadwear grade in a size, a two-line treadwear comparison, or a November 2026 rebate whose purchase window is on the maker’s own page. Above those, the earlier list still has eight sizes with fewer than ten graded lines, ten lines filed mostly as “All sizes,” Michelin load and speed charts read ${CHART_DATE}, and the November 27 and November 30, 2026 date pages. No prices are added.`;
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Exact lookups', href: LOOKUP_PATH }];
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Why do these sizes have their own pages?', a: 'Each of them has at least five graded lines in the NHTSA file and fewer than ten. A cutoff of ten lines leaves them unpublished. The ranking on each size page is only the lines NHTSA names for that size.' },
  { q: 'Why do these tire lines have their own pages?', a: 'The launch list keeps the 300 lines with the most records that name a specific size. These lines are filed mostly as “All sizes,” so that cutoff skips them even though the file has a treadwear grade.' },
  { q: 'Do the November pages list a sale price?', a: 'No. November 27, 2026 and November 30, 2026 are calendar dates. A maker rebate is included only when that maker’s own page states a purchase window that includes the day. Amounts stay in the maker’s words.' },
];
const ld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) }];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} crumbs={crumbs} ld={ld} og="lookup" modified={EXACT_DATE}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Exact match · wave 2</p>
  <h1>Exact tire size and line lookups</h1>
  <div class="answer">{answer}</div>

  <h2>Common sizes with fewer than ten graded lines</h2>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Size</th><th class="n">Graded lines</th><th>Pages</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{sizes.map((s) => <tr>
      <td><a href={sizeUrl(s.key)}>{s.label}</a></td>
      <td class="n">{s.lines}</td>
      <td><a href={sizeMeaningPath(s.key)}>What it means</a> · <a href={sizeCostPath(s.key)}>Cost per mile</a></td>
    </tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="tbl-note">Grades are NHTSA UTQG records that name the size. The cost page uses a price you type. All published sizes are on <a href="/sizes/">the size list</a>.</p>

  <h2>Tire lines the explicit-size cutoff skips</h2>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Line</th><th class="n">Median treadwear</th><th class="n">NHTSA records</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{lines.map((l) => <tr>
      <td><a href={lineUrl(l)}>{l.brand} {l.line}</a></td>
      <td class="n">{l.wear_median}</td>
      <td class="n">{l.records}</td>
    </tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="tbl-note">The median is the line’s NHTSA treadwear grades, not miles. Brand hubs are on <a href="/tires/">tire lines</a>.</p>

  <h2>Load index and speed rating</h2>
  <p>Charts read {CHART_DATE} from Michelin. <a href={LOAD_INDEX_PATH}>Load index chart</a>: {LOAD_PAGES.map((p, i) => <span><a href={loadIndexPath(p.code)}>{p.code}</a>{i < LOAD_PAGES.length - 1 ? ', ' : ''}</span>)}. <a href={SPEED_RATING_PATH}>Speed rating chart</a>: {SPEED_PAGES.map((r, i) => <span><a href={speedRatingPath(r.letter)}>{r.letter}</a>{i < SPEED_PAGES.length - 1 ? ', ' : ''}</span>)}. The rules page is <a href="/guides/load-index-and-speed-rating/">load index and speed rating</a>.</p>

  <h2>November 27 and November 30, 2026</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={blackFridayPath}>Black Friday 2026 tire rebate dates</a> (Friday, November 27).</li>
    <li><a href={cyberMondayPath}>Cyber Monday 2026 tire rebate dates</a> (Monday, November 30).</li>
    <li><a href={REBATE_PATH}>Rebate lookup</a> for every November and December 2026 window the maker pages stated. The lookup is not gated.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Mileage warranties</h2>
  <p>Each row is one tire line. Miles are the maker’s limited treadwear warranty, read {EXACT_DATE}. The NHTSA grade on the page is not those miles.</p>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Page</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{warrantyPages.map((p) => <tr><td><a href={exactPath(p.slug)}>{p.h1}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Highest treadwear grade by size</h2>
  <p>The page names the highest UTQG treadwear grade NHTSA filed for that exact size. It is not a mileage warranty. Some of these sizes have fewer than ten graded lines, so they are not in the main size list.</p>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Page</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{mileagePages.map((p) => <tr><td><a href={exactPath(p.slug)}>{p.h1}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Head-to-head treadwear</h2>
  <p>Two lines, their NHTSA grades, and a warranty cell only when a maker page is cited. Michelin’s own 2022 test is quoted only on the pairs that test included.</p>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Page</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{comparePages.map((p) => <tr><td><a href={exactPath(p.slug)}>{p.h1}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>November 2026 rebates, by maker</h2>
  <p>A page exists only when that maker’s own page states a purchase window that includes November 2026. Black Friday is November 27 and Cyber Monday is November 30. The maker pages do not use those names. No sale price is added.</p>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Page</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{rebatePages.map((p) => <tr><td><a href={exactPath(p.slug)}>{p.h1}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>

  <FaqList faqs={faqs} />
</Base>
